        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your 85-year-old female patient, admitted on 27/11/2018 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, pulse oximetry, and blood tests, confirming an acute exacerbation without pneumonia. Electrocardiography showed no acute cardiac pathology. Treatment consisted of inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, resulting in satisfactory clinical improvement. The patient was mobilised with physiotherapy support and received education regarding her condition and inhaler technique. She was discharged in a stable condition. Please continue outpatient COPD management and review her inhaler regimen accordingly. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
